.TH ONEDRIVE-ONDEMAND-RESYNC 1 "October 2026" "onedrive-ondemand" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
onedrive-ondemand-resync \- resynchronise a OneDrive Files On-Demand profile in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onedrive-ondemand-resync
[\fB\-\-no\-follow\fR] [\fIPROFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the systemd user unit \fBonedrive-ondemand-resync@\fIPROFILE\fB.service\fR.
\fIPROFILE\fR is the directory name below \fI~/.config\fR (default
\fBonedrive-ondemand\fR). The unit stops the profile's normal unit
(\fBonedrive-ondemand.service\fR for the default profile,
\fBonedrive-ondemand@\fIPROFILE\fB.service\fR otherwise), runs
\fBonedrive \-\-on-demand \-\-on-demand-resync-once\fR with the mount active,
and starts the normal unit again if the resync succeeded. If it failed, the
resync unit is left in the failed state and the normal unit stays stopped.
While the resync runs, the normal unit is skipped if something starts it.
.PP
By default the resync's journal is shown until it finishes, and the exit
status is that of the resync. Ctrl+C stops following; the resync continues.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-follow\fR
Only start the unit and return.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; the exit status of the client (or 1) on failure; 2 for usage
errors; 130 when following was interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR onedrive (1),
.BR onedrive-ondemand-setup (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
